      "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4A3Fne",
      "body": "I would prefer option to have your own VPN. You need to trust Tailscale regarding the privacy. And they are not immune to court orders. ",
      "author": {
        "login": "MatejKovacic",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3339198?u=cabb25f233a032a2e61dd63685a7220ce5bcfd8a&v=4",
        "url": "https://github.com/MatejKovacic"
      },
      "created_at": "2025-09-18T09:31:36Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-09-18T09:31:36Z",
      "is_answer": false,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4A3GOD",
          "body": "The combination of their clients being open source and [Tailnet Lock](https://tailscale.com/kb/1226/tailnet-lock) means I'm somewhat less concerned about privacy and court orders. [Headscale](https://headscale.net/stable/) is also a thing if you want to run your own copy of the server. But I see what you're saying, and to be clear I'm not suggesting we integrate this into Rayhunter officially! ",
          "author": {
            "login": "simonft",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6940?u=87e422ffd7a301cc6abbdb54e480726ba4c4eeca&v=4",
